From eb10ef582e7b3019d687bcd31a845acc2429d2bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: raawaa-engine <engine@raawaa.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:33:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(delivery): make Hama free for every payment method, other
 governorates $2

Owner-approved delivery contract (2026-11-07):
  Hama governorate  -> free delivery for COD and Sham Cash alike
  other governorates -> $2 for both payment methods
Product prices are untouched (13 / 16 / 25).

Root cause: the cart derived free delivery only from
`payment.methods[].freeDeliveryIn`, so COD in Hama was charged $2 while the
copy said free, and zone.fee drove every other surface. Free delivery is now
read from the zone fee itself as well:

- js/config.js: Hama zone fee 2 -> 0, notes/descriptions rewritten; the
  zero-fee rule is documented at the source so future edits stay coherent.
- js/cart.js: isFreeDelivery() treats a zero-fee zone as free for every
  payment method and keeps freeDeliveryIn for per-method exceptions; the
  payment-method description and the payment card now state both zones, so
  no surface claims a fee the cart does not charge.
- order-system/order-core.mjs + order-pricing.js: server-side pricing applies
  the same rule and returns `freeDelivery`, so a stored order can never
  disagree with the cart that produced it. order-entry bundle rebuilt.
- js/campaign.js and scripts/margin_calc.py: same rule in the campaign
  listing and margin tool.
- index.html, serum.html, hama.html, docs/HAMA-OPS-KIT-AR.md: remove every
  claim that Hama COD costs $2 or that free delivery is Sham-Cash-only.
- New scripts/delivery-contract.test.mjs: four-case regression
  (Hama/COD $0, Hama/Sham Cash $0, other/COD $2, other/Sham Cash $2) across
  the browser cart, the WhatsApp message and the server pricing engine, plus
  a copy guard that fails if any page re-states a Hama fee.
- Existing price/delivery assertions updated to the same contract.

Verification: npm run gates:offline -> 29 checks + 519 site checks, 238 unit
tests, 0 failures. No product price, homepage design or ad spend changed; no
deployment was performed.
